Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # v5.9
Signed-off-by: Yuto Ohnuki <ytohnuki@amazon.com>
Reviewed-by: Darrick J. Wong <djwong@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Carlos Maiolino <cem@kernel.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug is a use-after-free vulnerability in the xfsaild_push() function within fs/xfs/xfs_trans_ail.c. After xfsaild_push_item() calls iop_push(), the AIL lock may be dropped, allowing concurrent inode reclaim or dquot shrinker to free the log item. The subsequent tracepoint calls and the use of the lsn variable (obtained from lip->li_lsn) still dereference the log item pointer, leading to access of freed memory.

Here is the patch:
